  "node_id": "prop_6",
  "edition": "Newton, Principia, Andrew Motte trans., 1729 (Wikisource); Book I, Section II, Proposition VI; Plate 3, Figure 2.",
  "caption": "In a space void of resistance, the centripetal force in the middle of a nascent arc is as the versed sine directly and the square of the time inversely.",
  "n_steps": 4,
  "steps": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "gloss": "The centre S, the body at P, and the tiny nascent arc PQ pose the measurement problem."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "gloss": "The tangent ZPR is the forceless path; the versed sine measures how far the body falls from it."
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "gloss": "QR is drawn parallel to SP and QT perpendicular to SP, tying orbit geometry to the force direction."
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "gloss": "The force-measure solid SP²·QT²/QR is the master formula for every later proposition."
    }
  ],
